# Lucas C.S. <lucascs@protonmail.com> (2026-08-08)
# ::gentoo masks >=app-text/calibre-8.11.0 (profiles/package.mask, 2025-12-15)
# over the AI features upstream added in that release. The mask has held for
# eight months and pins ::gentoo's installable calibre at 8.9.0, six minor
# series and one major behind upstream.
#
# This overlay ships the current series instead. The AI code is opt-in by
# construction, not by policy: nothing under src/calibre/ai/ is imported until
# the user configures a backend, and Preferences->Tweaks carries
# hide_ai_features to remove the menu entries entirely. Of the seven backends
# upstream provides, two -- ollama and lm_studio -- talk only to localhost, so
# using the feature at all does not require handing text to a third party.
# Nothing here is enabled by default and nothing phones home on its own.
#
# The atom is deliberately UNqualified, which is the opposite of what the
# nodejs entry in profiles/package.mask needs, and for the same underlying
# reason. Portage stamps every repo-level atom with the repository being
# processed, and when it processes this overlay it re-reads the master's
# package.mask too -- so ::gentoo's calibre mask lands here twice, once as
# ">=app-text/calibre-8.11.0::gentoo" and once as "...::bentoo". The ::bentoo
# copy is the one that masks this overlay's ebuild, and only a bare atom
# (which Portage stamps ::bentoo in turn) cancels it. An explicit ::gentoo
# here cancels the wrong copy and leaves 9.13.0 masked -- measured.
#
# Leaving ::gentoo's own calibre ebuilds masked is intentional: this overlay
# ships the version it vouches for and does not unmask a master's packages.
#
# Remove this entry if ::gentoo lifts its mask.
>=app-text/calibre-8.11.0

# Lucas C.S. <lucascs@protonmail.com> (2026-08-21)
# ::gentoo masks =dev-lang/go-1.27.0 (profiles/package.mask, arthurzam,
# 2026-08-20, bug #981130) and additionally ships the ebuild with its KEYWORDS
# line commented out.  This overlay carries its own copy with KEYWORDS restored
# and cancels the inherited mask here.
#
# The tracker's three blockers are all third-party code depending on Go
# internals, not defects in the toolchain: net-p2p/kubo via cockroachdb/swiss
# linknaming runtime symbols (fixed upstream 2026-08-20, not yet tagged), and
# app-admin/vault at 1.15.6 and 1.18.4 carrying an x/tools copy older than the
# 2025-07-09 removal of internal/tokeninternal.  None of this overlay's twelve
# Go packages is exposed: no consumer of cockroachdb/swiss, every x/tools pin
# at v0.44.1 or newer, and dev-util/trivy the only importer of json/v2.
#
# Build risk was measured rather than assumed: this toolchain was installed
# locally from 2026-08-19 17:33 to 2026-08-20 19:58 and 38 Go packages -- among
# them docker, podman, containerd, terraform, github-cli, restic and cosign --
# rebuilt against it without a single failure.  What that does NOT cover is
# runtime: 1.27 backs encoding/json v1 with v2, which rejects invalid UTF-8 and
# duplicate object names v1 accepted.  That divergence surfaces on user data,
# never in emerge, and GOEXPERIMENT=nojsonv2 cannot pre-empt it -- the flag
# removes encoding/json/v2 and jsontext from the stdlib instead of swapping the
# implementation, so it is a per-package reaction and is unusable on anything
# importing json/v2.
#
# The atom is deliberately UNqualified, for the same reason the calibre entry
# above is.  Portage stamps every repo-level atom with the repository being
# processed, so ::gentoo's mask lands here twice, as "::gentoo" and as
# "::bentoo".  Only the ::bentoo copy masks this overlay's ebuild, and only a
# bare atom cancels it.
#
# Remove this entry, and dev-lang/go-1.27.0, once ::gentoo lifts its mask.
=dev-lang/go-1.27.0
